        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Stabilize Codex Computer Use readiness",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nCodex Computer Use readiness could go stale or look healthy when it was not actually usable. OpenClaw agents can run with isolated per-agent `CODEX_HOME` directories, so one agent could keep a stale cached Computer Use plugin even after the locally installed Codex.app bundle was updated. Status/setup also reported coarse plugin availability without separately proving installation, MCP exposure, and live `list_apps` behavior.\n\nThat is how a request could ask for Codex Computer Use while the runtime silently lacked a working Computer Use bridge or fell back to other automation without making the failure inspectable.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR hardens Codex Computer Use setup so OpenClaw no longer treats “plugin exists somewhere” as sufficient readiness.\n\nIt adds:\n\n- shared local bundled Computer Use plugin cache reconciliation for per-agent `CODEX_HOME` directories, defaulting to a symlink back to the locally installed Codex.app bundle and removing stale cached versions\n- decomposed `/codex computer-use status` results for installation, MCP exposure, and a live `computer-use.list_apps` probe\n- 60s live-probe timeout, exactly one 60s retry, and narrow auto-repair that only terminates stale `SkyComputerUseClient ... mcp` children\n- periodic per-shared-client Computer Use health probes on the configured 30/60/120/240 minute cadence, using the same live-probe and repair path\n- fail-closed setup behavior by default while keeping browser/DOM fallback available when explicitly requested outside the Computer Use setup path\n- config/schema/docs for `liveTestTimeoutMs`, `toolCallTimeoutMs`, `leaseTimeoutMs`, `healthCheckIntervalMinutes`, `pluginCacheMode`, `fallbackOnFailure`, and `autoRepair`\n- a window-scope Computer Use lease manager with renewal/preemption semantics for callers that can supply a stable window id\n- `openclaw doctor` surfacing for enabled Codex Computer Use, including configured health cadence and the status command to inspect installation/exposure/live-test layers\n\n## Context\n\nThis addresses the failure mode where one OpenClaw agent could keep using a stale per-agent Codex plugin cache even after Codex.app had a newer bundled Computer Use plugin, and where status/setup could report only coarse plugin availability instead of separating install state, MCP exposure, and live runtime health.\n\nThe previous direction in #96730 improved app-server command selection/startup behavior, but it did not make Computer Use readiness globally inspectable across agents, did not reconcile isolated per-agent plugin caches with the locally installed Codex.app bundle, and did not prove the MCP bridge with a real `list_apps` call before reporting readiness. This PR closes those gaps locally and offline; it does not depend on a remote marketplace.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe new lease manager is window-scoped by design, not app-scoped and not host-global. Native Codex MCP notifications are observational, so full pre-execution enforcement requires Computer Use tool payloads to expose a stable window identifier before the MCP call begins. The PR documents that boundary and adds the tested lease primitive for call sites that can provide that scope.\n\n## Evidence\n\nPost-rebase on `origin/main` (`8fa83d2742`), I verified the patch locally with targeted unit coverage, command formatting/doctor coverage, and TypeScript checks:\n\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-codex-app-server-support.config.ts extensions/codex/src/app-server/computer-use-health.test.ts extensions/codex/src/app-server/computer-use-cache.test.ts extensions/codex/src/app-server/computer-use-leases.test.ts` — 3 files, 8 tests passed\n- `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-codex-app-server-tools.config.ts extensions/codex/src/app-server/computer-use.test.ts extensions/codex/src/app-server/request.test.ts` — 2 files, 31 tests passed\n- `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-codex-app-server-runtime.config.ts extensions/codex/src/app-server/config.test.ts` — 1 file, 115 tests passed\n- `pnpm exec vitest run extensions/codex/src/app-server/attempt-startup.test.ts` — 1 file, 8 tests passed\n- `pnpm exec vitest run src/commands/doctor/shared/codex-route-warnings.test.ts extensions/codex/src/commands.test.ts` — 2 files, 244 tests passed\n- `pnpm tsgo:extensions:test`\n- `pnpm tsgo:core:test`\n",
        "branch": "fix/computer-use-shared-health",
